{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffsupervisor", "label": "BackoffSupervisor", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Die Default-Strategie startet ein Kind bis zu 10-mal pro Minute neu und wuerde damit eine kaputte Abhaengigkeit haemmern. Der BackoffSupervisor wickelt ein einzelnes Kind, spawnt es unter stoppingStrategy, death-watched es und plant den Respawn nach policy.delayFor(n). Fuer transiente Fehler, nicht fuer Programmierfehler.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffoptions", "label": "BackoffOptions<T>", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": null, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_triggeron", "label": "triggerOn (TerminationTrigger)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "'failure' ist richtig, wenn man 'Restart bei unerwartetem Tod' modelliert: ein sauberer Self-Stop ist eine bewusste Wahl, die der Supervisor ehren sollte. 'any' restartet bei jeder Terminierung, wenn der Supervisor sich nicht darum kuemmert, warum das Kind stoppte.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_forwardstrategy", "label": "forward: stash | drop", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Stashen erhaelt Sender-Refs, sodass Ask-Antworten nach dem Respawn weiter funktionieren. Verwerfen ist richtig fuer transiente Pings (Telemetrie, Heartbeats), wo veraltete Nachrichten schlimmer als verlorene sind.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_resetcounter", "label": "resetCounter", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Ohne Zuruecksetzen bekommt ein Kind, das nach einer lang stabilen Periode fehlschlaegt, dasselbe lange Backoff wie nach einem kuerzlichen Crash - meist falsch, weil der lang laufende Erfolg suggeriert, dass der Fehler frisch ist. 'after-min-stable' setzt zurueck, sobald das Kind mindestens minBackoff am Leben war.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_draingracems", "label": "drainGraceMs + forwardDuringGrace", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Schuetzt vor Kindern, die in preStart crashen: stirbt das Kind im Grace-Fenster, wird der Stash fuer die naechste Inkarnation zurueckgehalten statt in Dead Letters zu gehen. forwardDuringGrace: true tauscht ein winziges Dead-Lettering-Risiko gegen niedrigere Latenz auf dem Happy-Path.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_stash_buffer", "label": "Nachrichten-Puffer waehrend des Backoff-Fensters", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Aufeinanderfolgende Kinder heissen child-1, child-2, ... damit alte Terminierungen nicht mit neuen Spawns kollidieren. Gepufferte Nachrichten werden mit erhaltenen Original-Sender-Refs an das neue Kind geflusht.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_oneforonestrategy", "label": "OneForOneStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Cappt Restarts bei N pro Fenster, verzoegert aber nicht zwischen ihnen. Komplementaer zum BackoffSupervisor: kombiniert ergibt sich 'back off zwischen Restarts, aber gib nach 10 Versuchen komplett auf'.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_no_nesting", "label": "Backoff-Supervisor nicht schachteln", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Jede Ebene multipliziert die wahrgenommene Recovery-Verzoegerung. Einen Backoff-Supervisor an der Schicht verwenden, wo transiente Fehler tatsaechlich passieren; hoehere Schichten nutzen einfache Supervision.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffsupervisor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_policy_backoffpolicy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffsupervisor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_triggeron", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_forwardstrategy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_stash_buffer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_resetcounter", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffoptions", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_draingracems", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_stash_buffer", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_stash_buffer", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffsupervisor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffsupervisor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_oneforonestrategy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_no_nesting", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffsupervisor", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffsupervisor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_circuit_breaker_circuitbreaker", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_backoff_supervisor_backoffsupervisor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_patterns_retry_retry", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/patterns/backoff-supervisor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}